{%- comment -%}
  Authorization policy: test_principal_admin (Layer-2, app-owned; TEST fixture).
  Permits a tool only when the calling PRINCIPAL (the bearer's user, not the browser
  session) holds mcp.admin — the same permission that gates the operator console — so
  the coverage suite can prove the admin tier is invisible to a plain member.
  Fail-closed: anything short of a proven operator principal → deny.
  Contract: return { allow, reason }. Receives principal, agent, arguments, tool,
  delegation_mode.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  function is_admin = 'modules/mcp/queries/principal/can', principal: principal, do: 'mcp.admin'
  assign r = {}
  assign r['allow'] = is_admin
  if is_admin
    assign r['reason'] = 'admin'
  else
    assign r['reason'] = 'not_admin'
  endif
  return r
%}
